.SS Introduction

A \fBRaku\fR module for building \fBCMake\fR projects to make \fB\&.so\fR files and installing them in into a chosen install directory\&. Based on Distribution::Builder::Cmake [https://raku.land/zef:rawleyfowler/Distribution::Builder::Cmake] by \fBRawley Fowler\fR I have kept to the same licencing 
.SS Installation

.RS 4m
.EX
zef install Distribution::Builder::Cmake


.EE
.RE
.SS Usage

Assuming your Raku project keeps its CMake project in a folder called my\-cmake\-project, and your exported lib is my\-lib\&. Note, the final \&.so file will be lib{$my\-lib}\&.so\&. In your META6\&.json you'll add the following:

.RS 4m
.EX
{ 
    \&.\&.\&.
    "depends": [
        "Distribution::Builder::Cmake\-alt"
    ], 
    "builder": "Distribution::Builder::Cmake\-alt",
    "build": {
        "lib": "my\-lib",
        "src\-dir": "my\-cmake\-project",
        "install": "/usr/local/lib",
        "install\-local": "$*HOME/lib",
        "master\-lib\-version": "0\&.0\&.1",
        "lib\-versions": {
            "0": "0\&.0\&.1",
            "": "0"
        },
            "source":   "src",
            "log":      "path",
            "debug":    false
    }
    \&.\&.\&.
}



.EE
.RE
.P
Where 
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
lib is the name of your lib and is mandatory\&.
.RE
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
src\-dir is the location of your library and is mandatory it should be relative to the working directory or it can be an empty string or a "\&."
.RE
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
install is optional and specifies the location to install the libraries (lib{$lib}\&.so files) it should be an absolute path otherwise the install would achieve nothing (defaults to /usr/local/lib)\&. \fBNB\fR this field supports expandable patterns ~/, $*HOME/, $HOME/, {$*HOME}/ and {$HOME}/ all expand to the user home directory followed by a / and ~username will expand to usernames dome dir\&.
.RE
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
install\-local is optional and specifies the location to install the libraries if installing locally (lib{$lib}\&.so files) it should be a path inside the users users directory tree, otherwise the install would achieve nothing (defaults to $HOME/lib)\&. \fBNB\fR this field supports expandable patterns ~/, $*HOME/, $HOME/, {$*HOME}/ and {$HOME}/ all expand to the user home directory followed by a / and ~username will expand to usernames dome dir\&.
.RE
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
master\-lib\-version specifies the version number to put on the \&.so file (i\&.e\&. lib{$lib}\&.so\&.{$master\-lib\-version}) but you can leave it as an empty sting\&.
.RE
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
lib\-versions a collection of mappings to specify a list of symbolic links to the library\&. The example above would produce 
.RE
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m

